NAME
====

**augite** - generate static sites for Git repositories

SYNOPSIS
========

**augite** _subcommand_ _arguments_
**augite** [**-h** | **--help**]

DESCRIPTION
===========

**augite** generates static HTML pages for Git repositories, including commit
logs, diffs, file contents, references and Atom feeds. File pages can be
highlighted with TextMate grammars. The generated files can be served by a
web server without running Augite on each request.

The **git** executable must be available on `PATH`. Both bare repositories
and repositories with working trees can be used. Pages describe committed
content, rather than uncommitted changes in the working tree.

SUBCOMMANDS
===========

- `augite-setup(1)`:
  Sets or shows a repository's description, owner and clone URL.

- `augite-repo(1)`:
  Generates one repository's site.

- `augite-index(1)`:
  Generates an index page listing repositories.

OPTIONS
=======

- **-h**, **--help**:
  Prints a usage summary and exits. Each subcommand also accepts these
  options to show its own usage.

EXIT STATUS
===========

**augite** exits with status 0 on success, including when help is requested,
and status 1 on an error.

EXAMPLES
========

Set repository metadata, generate its pages and create an index:

````
$ augite setup -d "The Analytical Engine" --owner "Ada Lovelace" /var/git/engine.git
$ augite repo -o public/engine /var/git/engine.git
$ augite index -o public /var/git/engine.git
````

SEE ALSO
========

`augite-index(1)`, `augite-repo(1)`, `augite-setup(1)`, `git(1)`

